==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|ru|swé}}
{{dercat|ru|ine-bsl-pro|ine-pro|inh=2}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|свои}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*svojь}}.

Cognates include Latin [[suus]], Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ἕ}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|स्वतह्|'''स्व'''तह्|tr='''sva'''taḥ}}, and perhaps Old English {{m|ang|self|'''se'''lf}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-свой.ogg}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|ru|pronoun|cat2=possessive pronouns}}

# {{lb|ru|reflexive-possessive pronoun}} [[one's]] own; [[my]], [[his]], [[her]], [[its]], [[our]], [[your]], [[their]] ''(always refers to the subject of the clause)''
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[курить|курю́]] '''свою́''' [[сигара|сига́ру]].|I’m smoking '''my''' cigar.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[мы|Мы]] [[курить|ку́рим]] '''свои́''' [[сигара|сига́ры]].|We’re smoking '''our''' cigars.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[курить|ку́рит]] '''свою́''' [[сигара|сига́ру]].|He’s smoking '''his''' cigar ('''his own''').}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[курить|ку́рит]] [[его́]] [[сигара|сига́ру]].|He’s smoking his (the other guy’s) cigar.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[она|Она́]] [[курить|ку́рит]] '''свою́''' [[сигара|сига́ру]].|She’s smoking '''her''' cigar ('''her own''').}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[она|Она́]] [[курить|ку́рит]] [[её]] [[сигара|сига́ру]].|She’s smoking her (the other lady's) cigar.}}
# [[allied]], [[friendly]]
# [[peculiar]]

